#     A withdrawn pack's pins are dropped from this mirror and its slug is
#     named here instead. The slug stays reserved: no community Expansion may
#     claim it. Historical pin lines are NOT deleted from the canonical
#     registry in mypka-expansions. That registry is an append-only audit
#     record, and members who already hold a downloaded artifact must keep
#     being able to verify its bytes.
#
#     The notice under each slug below is the SOURCE TEXT for the WS-003 §2
#     RED verdict. Read it out; do not improvise around it.
#
# ---- slack, withdrawn 2026-07-27 --------------------------------------------
#     The Slack Expansion is discontinued and unsupported. It receives no
#     further updates, and there is no newer version to move to: the
#     supported path is to retire it, not to upgrade.
#
#     This is NOT a security advisory. No vulnerability was found in the
#     pack, nothing was exploited, and no data leaked. It is retired because
#     an always-on background listener holding live Slack workspace tokens is
#     more than myICOR is willing to keep standing behind.
#
#     Nothing is being taken away from you. If you already have it installed
#     it keeps running until you retire it yourself, on your own timing. This
#     notice is the record, and it lives here in your own folder; there is no
#     separate announcement to wait for.
#
#     If you are still running it, three steps, in this order. Step 2 is the
#     one that matters: deleting local files revokes nothing, so skipping it
#     leaves a live bot token in your Slack workspace indefinitely.
#       1. Stop the listener. Run Expansions/slack/scripts/uninstall.sh if you
#          still have it. Otherwise unload the launch agent:
#          launchctl unload ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.mypka.slack-listener.plist
#          and delete that plist. If you started it by hand, Ctrl+C is enough.
#       2. Revoke the tokens AT SLACK. Open api.slack.com/apps, select your
#          app, and delete it. That invalidates the xoxb bot token and the
#          xapp app-level token in one move and removes the bot from your
#          workspace. Deleting the local .env does none of this: a copy
#          survives in Time Machine and the bot stays installed.
#       3. Clear local artifacts. Expansions/slack/, and, if you do not want
#          the captured message history, Team Inbox/slack-incoming/,
#          Team Inbox/slack-outgoing/, and /tmp/mypka-slack-listener.log/.err.
#     WS-003 §Uninstall walks the scaffold side of this with you.
slack WITHDRAWN 2026-07-27 reason=discontinued-by-myicor
